0result.sql is more precise because it:

1. Calculates each user’s exact current age by checking whether the birthday has already occurred this year (subtracts the extra 1 when `strftime('%m‑%d','now') < strftime('%m‑%d', birth_date)`).
2. Groups on that age value and therefore places users in the correct decade bucket.
3. Uses the same result set as 1result.sql but avoids the systematic +1‐year bias that 1result.sql has for users whose birthdays are later in the year.

```plaintext
0result.sql
```